"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both AMD and NVIDIA disclose the risk associated with the rapidly evolving nature of their markets and the necessity of timely product adaptation. AMD states that 'The markets in which our products are sold are highly competitive and rapidly evolving' and success depends on introducing 'products on a timely basis.' NVIDIA states that its platforms experience 'rapid changes in technology, customer requirements... and industry standards' and success depends on the ability to 'timely identify industry changes, adapt our strategies, and develop new or enhance... products.' Both identify the speed of technological change as a key business driver and risk factor.",
